{
  "id": 529721818,
  "iid": 26434,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "OpenVPN: Validate wrapped client key length against remaining bytes",
  "description": "Summary:\n\nIn OpenVPN dissection, wkc_len was extracted without validating that it does not exceed msg_length_remaining. When wkc_len is larger than the remaining message length, data_len becomes negative, throwing a dissector exception in proto_tree_add_item() and aborting packet dissection.\n\nChanges:\n\n\\- Added validation ensuring parsed_wkc_len is at least 2 bytes and does not exceed msg_length_remaining.\n\n\\- Used uint32_t for parsed_wkc_len to match msg_length_remaining and prevent sign-comparison compiler warnings.\n\n\\- Verified with tools/check_apis.py (0 warnings) and checked with -Werror=sign-compare.",
  "state": "merged",
  "created_at": "2026-09-09T04:30:20.643Z",
  "updated_at": "2026-09-10T13:23:18.457Z",
