    {
      "id": "ee57bc44f17ade54faa640ef37331465e7af678d",
      "short_id": "ee57bc44",
      "created_at": "2026-09-09T04:29:48.000+00:00",
      "parent_ids": [
        "857d9b98e9d70c0f0666bea18c3b2b060e5bd93b"
      ],
      "title": "OpenVPN: Validate wrapped client key length against remaining bytes",
      "message": "OpenVPN: Validate wrapped client key length against remaining bytes\n\nIn OpenVPN packets with P_CONTROL_HARD_RESET_CLIENT_V3 or P_CONTROL_WKC_V1 opcodes, wkc_len is read from the last 2 bytes of the packet without checking if it exceeds the remaining payload length. If wkc_len is larger than msg_length_remaining, data_len becomes negative, causing an exception in proto_tree_add_item.\n\nUse uint32_t parsed_wkc_len to validate that the key length is at least 2 bytes and does not exceed msg_length_remaining.",
      "author_name": "meel-ayush",
      "author_email": "ayushmeel.dev@gmail.com",
      "authored_date": "2026-09-09T04:29:48.000+00:00",
      "committer_name": "meel-ayush",
